      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="86" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y = \frac{1}{\sqrt{x + 1}},x = 0, x = 3, \text{and} y = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="87" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x = \sec (y) \text{and} y = \frac{\pi}{4}, y = 0 \text{and} x = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$\pi \pi$$ units3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="88" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y = \frac{1}{x + 1},x = 0, , x = 2, \text{and} y = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="89" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y = 4 - x,y = x, \text{and} x = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$16\pi 316\pi 3$$ units3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, draw the region bounded by the curves. Then, find the volume when the region is rotated around the x-axis.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="90" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y = x + 2,y = x + 6,x = 0, \text{and} x = 5$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
