        <paragraph>$$26\pi 26\pi$$ units3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, draw the region bounded by the curves. Then, use the washer method to find the volume when the region is revolved around the y-axis.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="98" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y = \sqrt{x},x = 4, \text{and} y = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="99" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y = x + 2,y = 2x - 1, \text{and} x = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$9\pi 9\pi$$ units3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="100" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y = \sqrt[3]{x} \text{and} y = x^{3}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="101" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x = e^{2y},x = y^{2},y = 0, \text{and} y = \ln (2)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$\pi 20(75-4ln5(2))\pi 20(75-4ln5(2))$$ units3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="102" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x = \sqrt{9 - y^{2}},x = e^{-y},y = 0, \text{and} y = 3$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="103" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Yogurt containers can be shaped like frustums. Rotate the line $$y = \frac{1}{m}x$$ around the y-axis to find the volume between $$y = a \text{and} y = b.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$m2\pi 3(b3-a3)m2\pi 3(b3-a3)$$ units3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="104" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Rotate the ellipse $$\left( {x^{2}/a^{2}} \right) + \left( {y^{2}/b^{2}} \right) = 1$$ around the x-axis to approximate the volume of a football, as seen here.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="105" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Rotate the ellipse $$\left( {x^{2}/a^{2}} \right) + \left( {y^{2}/b^{2}} \right) = 1$$ around the y-axis to approximate the volume of a football.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$4a2b\pi 34a2b\pi 3$$ units3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="106" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>A better approximation of the volume of a football is given by the solid that comes from rotating $$y = \sin x$$ around the x-axis from $$x = 0$$ to $$x = \pi.$$ What is the volume of this football approximation, as seen here?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="107" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>What is the volume of the Bundt cake that comes from rotating $$y = \sin x$$ around the y-axis from $$x = 0$$ to $$x = \pi?$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2\pi 22\pi 2$$ units3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, find the volume of the solid described.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="108" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>The base is the region between $$y = x$$ and $$y = x^{2}.$$ Slices perpendicular to the x-axis are semicircles.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="109" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>The base is the region enclosed by the generic ellipse $$\left( {x^{2}/a^{2}} \right) + \left( {y^{2}/b^{2}} \right) = 1.$$ Slices perpendicular to the x-axis are semicircles.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2ab2\pi 32ab2\pi 3$$ units3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="110" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Bore a hole of radius $$a$$ down the axis of a right cone of height $$b$$ and radius $$b$$ through the base of the cone as seen here.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="111" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the volume common to two spheres of radius $$r$$ with centers that are $$2h$$ apart, as shown here.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$V=2\pi 3(2r+h)r-h2V=2\pi 3(2r+h)r-h2$$ units3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="112" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the volume of a spherical cap of height $$h$$ and radius $$r$$ where $$h &lt; r,$$ as seen here.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="113" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the volume of a sphere of radius $$R$$ with a cap of height $$h$$ removed from the top, as seen here.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$\pi 3(h+R)(h-2R)2\pi 3(h+R)(h-2R)2$$ units3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
  </exercises>
</section>
